[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Voltage-scaled current-controlled transport groundwork

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This is a bounded native/API prerequisite, not an original-deck closure and not
a complete Gummel-Poon model. Fresh original rtlinv still refuses; its full stock
program also emits obsolete-option and missing-print-vector diagnostics. Fresh
temper-1/temper-3 already pass and are not recounted. Temper-2 fails one stock
voltage bound although its original ratio assertion passes: independent Shockley
KCL bisection from the effective requested model gives0.4052203046185694V at40C,
matching our result, while stock gives0.4053120303623846V. No accuracy degradation,
refined-control result or relaxed bound is accepted as original-default closure.

Pinned RSpice rspice-core-devices/device/semiconductor/bjt/intrinsic/charge.rs
shows both1/qb transport and TF*IFI/qb stored charge with Vbc derivatives. A
transport-gain-only BJT VA promotion would therefore drop dynamic physics. Keep
BJT frontend admission unchanged until charge/base-resistance assumptions are
traced and independently qualified. This slice supplies one reusable memoryless
product law, with no implicit BJT approximation or parameter aliases.

Reuse existing current-control branch resolution, four-terminal conductance
stamping, finite Newton state and converged-bias sparse AC. The previous retained
Rust/SpiceSharp/ngspice reuse assessment still applies. Existing static CCCS gain
cannot represent the required voltage partial; the single-voltage expression
model cannot read an MNA branch current. No new production library or legacy
runtime is needed for this small typed constitutive law.

Affected producers/consumers: Rust/.NET element wire contract, structural and
branch validation, immutable compile plan, residual/Jacobian, sparse AC bias,
independent current/power audits, scalar-variation refusal and capability/schema
metadata. Control current is the existing voltage-defined P-to-N branch unknown;
control voltage is Vcp-Vcn. Both controls draw no additional current. Output is
P-to-N amperes. Gain is dimensionless; voltage coefficient is inverse volts.
No hidden storage or source branch is created. Native transient support and all
BJT charge semantics remain separately unqualified.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-VOLTAGE-SCALED-CCCS-LAW-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Finite owned product current law
STATEMENT: >>>
The model shall impose Iout=gain*Icontrol*(1+coefficient*Vcontrol), with exact
partials gain*(1+coefficient*Vcontrol) and gain*Icontrol*coefficient. Finite signed
parameters and states shall preserve their physical polarity. Nonfinite data,
intermediate/result overflow and unresolved branch controls shall fail without
clamps, zero substitution or successful partial output.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: voltage_scaled_cccs, circuit::Element and immutable
compiled current model. Verification: analytical derivatives, malformed wire and
model cases, reproducible proptest and independent native/API DC/AC examples.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-VOLTAGE-SCALED-CCCS-STAMPS-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Exact coupled-current residual and incremental stamps
STATEMENT: >>>
The model shall stamp P/N residual signs and both branch-current and control-
voltage Jacobian columns. Sparse AC shall use both partials at a converged DC
bias. Aliased terminals shall accumulate; the model shall add no branch unknown
or charge. Independent DC current/power audits shall evaluate the physical law.
Where public bias is unavailable, the nonlinear AC audit shall say not_checked.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: LU/Faer analytical DC and both AC gains, full MNA finite differences,
sparse/dense equality, alias feedback, corruption audits and physical oracle.
This prerequisite does not authorize BJT frontend admission or original counts.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-VOLTAGE-SCALED-CCCS-WIRE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Typed transport wire boundary
STATEMENT: >>>
The Rust/.NET element and request schema shall identify output/control nodes,
branch control identity, finite gain and voltage coefficient. Unknown fields,
wrong field types, invalid node bounds and missing branch controls shall refuse.
The model shall not masquerade as an independently variable scalar CCCS gain.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: circuit, Client Requests, compile, variation and request
schema. Verification: actual serializer/native entry point and maintained
schema validator. Resource/domain validity remains the runtime's responsibility.
<<<
